From e99e5239ef23c955395a63ab27d640e19f73e7df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] laptop-detect.in: guard power_supply ls with 2>/dev/null

On HarmonyOS the /sys/class/power_supply directory EXISTS but is not
readable (EACCES): the unguarded `ls` leaks "Permission denied" to
stderr and the loop silently iterates nothing. Every other probe in
this script already carries a 2>/dev/null guard; this line is the one
upstream omission. On GNU/Linux the directory is either absent or
readable, so the patch changes nothing there.

--- a/laptop-detect.in
+++ b/laptop-detect.in
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@
 /sbin/modprobe battery 2> /dev/null || true
 sysfs_power_supply=/sys/class/power_supply
 if [ -d $sysfs_power_supply ]; then
-	for power_supply in $(ls $sysfs_power_supply)
+	for power_supply in $(ls $sysfs_power_supply 2>/dev/null)
 	do
 		if (
 			grep -q Battery $sysfs_power_supply/$power_supply/type 2>/dev/null
--
